            pathophysiologyEn = "4 Phases of Nociception & Gate Control Theory:\n1. Transduction: Noxious stimuli convert to electrical impulses via prostaglandins, bradykinin, substance P.\n2. Transmission: A-delta (fast, sharp) and C-fibers (slow, dull) carry impulses to dorsal horn and thalamus.\n3. Perception: Cerebral cortex interprets pain consciously.\n4. Modulation: Descending inhibitory pathways (endorphins, serotonin) & Melzack-Wall Gate Control Theory ('gating' impulses in the spinal dorsal horn).",
